## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design runtime SLA guarantees under multi-tenant load, focusing on scheduling, backpressure, and cross-tenant fairness in data delivery to external sinks like Snowflake.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant scheduling and backpressure
- SLA-driven latency budgeting
- Memory- and time-bounded queues
- Canary and burst testing in production-like loads

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst; // max tokens in bucket
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  consume(n) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

